1
00:00:00,029 --> 00:00:03,119
Work orders keep an assignment
and its updates together.

2
00:00:03,589 --> 00:00:08,819
Start by reading the intended order, its
status, priority, station and due date.

3
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:13,380
This recorded example is Training
Only, Assigned software practice.

4
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:18,270
It is Assigned, has Normal priority,
uses the Inspection type and names

5
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:20,450
Firehouse fifty-one as its station.

6
00:00:20,879 --> 00:00:23,850
The description makes it a
fictional software exercise.

7
00:00:24,329 --> 00:00:27,409
Read the Steps section before
accepting responsibility

8
00:00:27,409 --> 00:00:28,819
for the intended assignment.

9
00:00:28,989 --> 00:00:32,059
Accept assignment is the
green action below Steps.

10
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:36,349
Change status is a separate section
with its own Update status button.

11
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:39,390
Log hours and Save hours
are separate again.

12
00:00:39,779 --> 00:00:43,329
These controls answer different
questions: accepting an assignment,

13
00:00:43,569 --> 00:00:45,820
recording its progress and logging time.

14
00:00:46,269 --> 00:00:49,589
Read the action you intend to
take rather than using a status

15
00:00:49,619 --> 00:00:52,759
or time entry as a substitute
for accepting the right work.The

16
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:56,419
next view previews On
hold in Change status.

17
00:00:56,740 --> 00:01:00,779
A Reason field appears below that
choice, followed by Update status.

18
00:01:01,129 --> 00:01:05,590
The order header still says Assigned;
selecting a proposed status in the form

19
00:01:05,619 --> 00:01:07,599
is different from saving that change.

20
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:11,939
Use a clear reason when a permitted
hold is appropriate for actual work.

21
00:01:12,219 --> 00:01:15,590
Here we are reviewing the offered
fields without submitting a hold.

22
00:01:15,759 --> 00:01:19,579
The Completed form presents
What was done to fix it, Cause

23
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,399
and All steps are complete.

24
00:01:21,759 --> 00:01:26,119
The switch is off in this recorded
preview, and Update status is below it.

25
00:01:26,570 --> 00:01:30,850
These fields help explain a completion
decision; they should reflect the actual

26
00:01:30,850 --> 00:01:33,200
work and your department's review process.

27
00:01:33,569 --> 00:01:37,430
This exercise inspects the fields
without declaring that an inspection

28
00:01:37,430 --> 00:01:39,020
or repair has been completed.

29
00:01:39,179 --> 00:01:43,100
After reviewing the available forms,
return to the intended assignment.

30
00:01:43,440 --> 00:01:45,699
Check its title and Assigned status again.

31
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:49,309
For this software exercise,
use Accept assignment.

32
00:01:49,649 --> 00:01:53,779
Keep that choice separate from submitting
the earlier hold or completion previews.

33
00:01:54,140 --> 00:01:58,119
The next screen will be used to verify
what was actually recorded, rather than

34
00:01:58,119 --> 00:02:00,099
treating a button press as the result.

35
00:02:00,269 --> 00:02:04,560
The recorded Activity section now
contains Assignment accepted and a

36
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:09,170
later Status changed to In progress
entry, each with a timestamp.

37
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:12,170
Change status currently shows In progress.

38
00:02:12,559 --> 00:02:16,189
Acceptance and the progress transition
are separate recorded events.

39
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:20,549
Read those events when handing work over
or checking who has taken responsibility.

40
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:24,809
Log hours, comment and photo
controls remain available, but this

41
00:02:24,809 --> 00:02:28,289
walkthrough verifies the recorded
acceptance and progress only.

42
00:02:28,450 --> 00:02:32,189
The same assignment review helps
security teams coordinate post equipment

43
00:02:32,189 --> 00:02:37,120
issues, wildland contractors organize
crew support, and industrial emergency

44
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:39,219
teams track standby equipment work.

45
00:02:39,670 --> 00:02:42,830
Search-and-rescue teams can
coordinate support tasks, while

46
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:46,309
community paramedicine and mental
health response teams can manage

47
00:02:46,309 --> 00:02:48,180
appropriate outreach support work.

48
00:02:48,619 --> 00:02:52,639
Fire and EMS departments can use the
same process for their assignments.

49
00:02:53,100 --> 00:02:56,830
Read the intended work, use the
appropriate action and verify

50
00:02:56,830 --> 00:02:58,910
Activity before the next handover.

